<title>BELGIUM: Belgian yr/yr inflation 1.97 pct in Sept.</title>
<headline>Belgian yr/yr inflation 1.97 pct in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economic Affairs Ministry released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES	Sept	August    Sept 1995</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 123.02     123.27     120.64</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	-0.20	 0.24	-0.26</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   1.97	 1.92	 1.19</p>
<p>    Health index *		  120.81     121.17</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.30	 0.27</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco, alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for liquid fuels and public transport, while prices for foreign trips and fresh fruit were lower.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
